A constraint near-miss on a template that ALSO has a free, input-only type
parameter. Conv pins T from its Box[T] result and lifts U (the type of its u
parameter) into the injector. Box[int] is a near-miss (int is not a Stringer),
so it becomes an input; Conv still serves Box[Name]. The lift must happen exactly
once: the doomed Box[int] attempt speculatively lifts a parameter, but that lift
is rolled back and the binding is memoized, so no phantom type parameter leaks
into the signature. The retained lifted parameter is named U, not U2: the
rolled-back attempt releases the name it reserved (liftedNames is rolled back
alongside liftedMeta), so the surviving lift reuses U.
-- config --
import-path: example.com/app
package-name: app
output: plumb_gen.go
-- example.com/app/a.go --
package app

type Stringer interface{ String() string }

type Name string

func (n Name) String() string { return string(n) }

type Box[T any] struct{ V T }

//plumb:build
func Conv[T Stringer, U any](u U) Box[T] { return Box[T]{} }

//plumb:build
func UseName(b Box[Name]) int { return 0 }

//plumb:build
func UseInt(b Box[int]) string { return "" }
